(OSWindowDriver << #OSWebDriver slots: #(#window #windows #inputSemaphore #interruptSemaphore #eventBuffer #eventProcess #interruptProcess #pendingEvents); sharedVariables: #(); package: 'OSWindow-Web') install!(OSNullBackendWindow << #OSWebBackendWindow slots: #(#lastPosition #modifierState #buttonState #clipboardText #pastedText #driver); sharedVariables: #(); package: 'OSWindow-Web') install!(OSWindowFormRenderer << #OSWebFormRenderer slots: #(#blits #blitPixels #presents); sharedVariables: #(); package: 'OSWindow-Web') install!!OSWebDriver commentStamp: '' prior: 0!I am the OSWindow driver of the Pharo world in a web page. The WebAssembly VM runs in a Web Worker, and the page owns the canvas. My only contact with the page is the WebDisplayPlugin, a builtin plugin of that VM, plus the interrupt semaphore of its WebHostPlugin.I am suitable only when the page provides a display (primitiveWebDisplayIsAvailable), so the node VM, the Console page and native VMs never pick me. Natively every primitive fails and its fallback code runs instead, which keeps me testable on a desktop VM: #pushEvent: then stands in for the page.My class-side #startUp: is registered with the SessionManager. The stock image saves OSSDL2Driver as the driver class, so I install myself before the world opens whenever the page provides a display.My class side also sets an image up for the web VMs (#setUpImage), when this package is loaded at build time and when the page files it in, and numbers this package (#packageVersion): the page sets up again, once, an image saved with an older version.The page queues its input as records of 8 integers:	type, timestamp, x, y, button | keySym | width, modifiers | (buttons << 8), scanCode | codePoint | dx | height, repeat | dyTypes: 1 mouse move, 2 button press, 3 button release, 4 wheel, 5 key down, 6 key up, 7 text input (one code point), 8 resize, 9 focus (button field 1 in, 0 out), 10 close, 11 save request.Modifiers: 1 shift, 2 ctrl, 4 alt, 8 cmd; text input ignores them, as with SDL. Press and release number the button as SDL does (1 left, 2 middle, 3 right), and the held buttons are SDL masks (1 left, 2 middle, 4 right). A resize to less than one pixel keeps one.My event loop runs at lowIOPriority and waits on the input semaphore, which webdisplay_push_event() signals. Alt, Ctrl or Cmd with the period key, and the page's Stop button (vm_interrupt(), which signals my interrupt semaphore), interrupt the busy process as the user interrupt key does on desktop VMs. A save request snapshots the image; the worker then stores it.The page has one canvas. It shows the newest of my windows that handles events, as the world and the Emergency Debugger do (a window opened without an event handler stays behind it), and that window gets the input. When it is destroyed, the one shown before comes back.!!OSWebBackendWindow commentStamp: '' prior: 0!I am the backend of the Pharo world's window in a web page, where the page draws my canvas. I turn the page's event records into OSWindow events (see OSWebDriver for their layout), and pass title, clipboard, cursor and focus requests to the page through the WebDisplayPlugin.My extent is that of the canvas in CSS pixels, so is the position of the mouse, and my screenScaleFactor is 1: the world has the size of the canvas on every display. The page also reports the canvas in device pixels (#pixelExtent), which my renderer answers as its outputExtent: OSWorldRenderer then takes devicePixelRatio for its canvasScaleFactor, and draws the world that much larger, one pixel per device pixel, as on a Retina display with SDL.As with SDL, keys and text are separate events: the page sends text input only for the keys that type a character, so Escape and the shortcuts reach Morphic as key downs, and text input reaches Morphic without modifiers.The page shows one window at a time (see OSWebDriver): only that one draws, and when it comes back after another one, it draws itself whole again.!!OSWebFormRenderer commentStamp: '' prior: 0!I copy the Pharo world's Form to the page's canvas. The Form has the canvasScaleFactor of OSWorldRenderer times the size of the world, which my outputExtent makes devicePixelRatio: the page shows it one pixel per device pixel. Each damaged rectangle is blitted into the RGBA frame of the WebDisplayPlugin, and the frame is then presented once per Morphic cycle; the page paints it when the VM returns to the worker. The frame is the page's only one: I draw only while the page shows my window (OSWebBackendWindow>>#isShown).Natively the primitives fail, and I only count what the page would have received (see #stats).!!AthensCairoSurface methodsFor: '*OSWindow-Web'!asForm	"A Form of my extent holding a copy of my pixels as they are now, the premultiplied ARGB32 of cairo, as the Form of the stock method holds them through the SurfacePlugin (see AthensCairoSurface class>>#registerSurface:): drawing it gives the same pixels. The Form is kept in my id slot, which the SurfacePlugin left free, and reused while my extent is the same, so a Form answered earlier takes my newer pixels at each call, where the stock one always shows them. My resource data, taken while the id slot was still nil, does not hold the Form: finalizing me keeps no copy of my pixels"	| form |	self checkSession.	self flush.	form := id.	(form isForm and: [ form extent = self extent ]) ifFalse: [		form := Form extent: self extent depth: 32.		id := form ].	"(the rows of a 32-bit format have 4 bytes a pixel and no padding, as the Form's have: the minimum only keeps a surface of another format from writing past the Form)"	LibC		memCopy: self getDataPtr		to: form bits		size: (self stride * self height min: form bits byteSize).	^ form! !!AthensCairoSurface class methodsFor: '*OSWindow-Web'!registerSurface: anAthensCairoSurface	"The web VMs have no SurfacePlugin, through which the stock method shares the pixels of a surface with BitBlt, and fails without: register nothing, and answer nil for the id slot of the surface, where #asForm keeps a copy of the pixels instead. Natively the prepared image takes this path too"	self checkSession.	^ nil! !!AthensCairoSurface class methodsFor: '*OSWindow-Web'!unregisterSurfaceWithId: anAthensCairoSurfaceId	"Nothing was registered (see #registerSurface:)"! !!OSWebBackendWindow methodsFor: 'accessing'!clipboardText	"Answer the latest of the text pasted into the page and the text copied in the image. A copy replaces the page's text too (primitiveWebSetClipboardText), so while that text is the one seen after the last copy, nothing was pasted since. The page sends UTF-8, but a paste must not open a debugger: bytes that are not UTF-8, or a sequence that the end cuts, read as question marks"	| pasted |	pasted := self primClipboardText ifNil: [ #[  ] ].	pasted = pastedText ifTrue: [ ^ clipboardText ].	^ [ pasted utf8Decoded ]		  on: ZnInvalidUTF8 , ZnIncomplete		  do: [ :error | error resume ]! !!OSWebBackendWindow methodsFor: 'accessing'!clipboardText: aString	"The browser may refuse to write the system clipboard, and a copy must still paste in Pharo, as it must natively, where the primitives fail: keep the copy, and the page's text as it is after the copy"	clipboardText := aString ifNil: [ '' ] ifNotNil: [ aString asString ].	self primSetClipboardText: clipboardText utf8Encoded.	pastedText := self primClipboardText ifNil: [ #[  ] ]! !!OSWebBackendWindow methodsFor: 'event handling'!deliver: anOSEvent	(anOSEvent respondsTo: #modifiers) ifTrue: [		self fillModifiers: anOSEvent modifiers ].	^ anOSEvent deliver! !!OSWebBackendWindow methodsFor: 'initialization'!destroy	"OSWindow>>#destroy: the page shows the window it showed before again"	| owner |	owner := driver.	driver := nil.	owner ifNotNil: [ owner windowDestroyed: self ]! !!OSWebBackendWindow methodsFor: 'accessing'!driver: anOSWebDriver	driver := anOSWebDriver! !!OS